3. C6 = C2 x C3 SUBFIELD LATTICE INSIDE Q(zeta_7)
C2 coordinate=quadratic character chi7, fixed field Q(sqrt(-7)).
C3 coordinate=quotient by complex conjugation +/-1, fixed field Q(cos(2pi/7)).
  sigma_1: chi7= 1 real_pair=(1, 6) fixes_Qsqrt_minus7=True fixes_real_cubic=True
  sigma_2: chi7= 1 real_pair=(2, 5) fixes_Qsqrt_minus7=True fixes_real_cubic=False
  sigma_3: chi7=-1 real_pair=(3, 4) fixes_Qsqrt_minus7=False fixes_real_cubic=False
  sigma_4: chi7= 1 real_pair=(3, 4) fixes_Qsqrt_minus7=True fixes_real_cubic=False
  sigma_5: chi7=-1 real_pair=(2, 5) fixes_Qsqrt_minus7=False fixes_real_cubic=False
  sigma_6: chi7=-1 real_pair=(1, 6) fixes_Qsqrt_minus7=False fixes_real_cubic=True
c3_pair_order_under_times3_mod14=[(1, 13), (3, 11), (5, 9)]
each_binding_pair_has_one_QR_and_one_NQR=True
readout=the C3 binding-pair quotient and the Q(sqrt(-7)) quadratic character are transverse sidecars.

4. TWO-PRIME PROOF PACKET
binding_layer = U, quotient by +/- gives the C3 orbit seeded by HYP-2909
covering_layer = 2U plus ramified apex7; 2U is the 2-adic shadow of U
hinge = 12 -> 24 is a height/doubling lift: it contains the old 12-kill lattice and adds interleaved 24-kills
guardrail = residue equality alone is false proof currency; same-residue height lifts can be strict positive rows
proof_target = prove unit-contact rigidity, then prove the covering-flex manifold has only AP/GW integer points

5. TOURNAMENT ANALYSIS OVER PROOF CARRIERS
pairwise_observable=preserved LRC predicate, binding detection, covering detection, field-lattice payload, rigidity target, proof readiness
binary_gauge=A->B iff weighted proof-carrier score(A)>score(B); tie Hamiltonian path is lexicographic
vertices=9
score_hist={29: 1, 42: 1, 50: 1, 54: 1, 58: 1, 60: 1, 61: 1, 62: 1, 73: 1}
directed_3cycles=0
hamiltonian_path_count=1
selected_path=crt_packet_U_plus_2U_plus_ramified7 -> c6_subfield_lattice_Qzeta7 -> c3_real_cubic_binding_pair_orbit -> apex7_ramified_covering_switch -> two_adic_unit_to_even_shadow_2U -> quadratic_Qsqrt_minus7_transverse_character -> hinge_12_to_24_height_lift -> raw_mod14_residue_table -> slogan_binding_units_covering_evens

6. NEXT PROOF OBLIGATIONS
A. Formalize unit-contact rigidity: tight rows retaining all six unit contacts force the C3 unit skeleton.
B. Add the transverse Q(sqrt(-7)) character as a sidecar, not a replacement for the C3 quotient.
C. Prove the covering layer 2U+{7} has a one-dimensional height flex and that its only integer tight lift is 12->24.
D. Combine with HYP-3265/HYP-3300: killed unit contacts must route to off-unit covering/Morse chamber witnesses.
